# NDR ABSOLUTE-VALUE vehicle (requirement R1, the half phase 1 left out).
#
# `def_ndr` takes the multiplier form only today (`width x2`), and an
# absolute value is a hard error naming that form.  The multiplier is
# PATTERN-INDEPENDENT — `x2` means "two signal slots" on every layer — which
# is why it shipped first.  An absolute value is the opposite: it means one
# PHYSICAL width, and how many slots that costs depends on the layer.
#
# This vehicle exists to pin that difference.  Its stack deliberately mixes
# pitches: M3/M5 carry 12 signal slots of (width 1 + space 1) between their
# rails, M4/M6 carry 12 of (width 2 + space 2).
#
# The divisor is the layer's PER-SIGNAL-SLOT CHANNEL COST (LayerStack's
# bit_pitch = unit_pitch / n_signal_slots), not the raw slot pitch: it
# amortizes the power rails across the signal slots, and it is what
# eff_bus_width already charges — so an absolute rule and the width model
# agree by construction rather than by coincidence.  Here that is
# 30/12 = 2.5 on M3/M5 and 60/12 = 5.0 on M4/M6.
#
#   fine3   width 3   -> M3/M5: ceil(3/2.5) = 2 slots.  M4/M6: ceil(3/5) = 1.
#   space5  width 4   -> M3/M5: ceil(4/2.5) = 2.       M4/M6: ceil(4/5) = 1.
#           spacing 5 -> M3/M5: ceil(5/2.5) - 1 = 1 guard.  M4/M6: 0.
#
# So ONE declaration resolves to DIFFERENT slot counts per layer — the thing
# no multiplier can express, and the reason R1 asks for the form at all.
#
# THE ROUNDING DECISION this vehicle fixes: an absolute value that falls
# BETWEEN slot counts rounds UP.  That is the phase-1 convention already
# applied to multipliers (`width x1.5` pays 2 slots — "conservative, never
# illegal"), and the alternative — refusing a value that does not land
# exactly on a slot boundary — would make a rule un-portable across exactly
# the mixed-pitch stack this vehicle is built from.  `space5`'s spacing on
# M3/M5 (5 / 2.5 = exactly 2) is the boundary case: it must pay 2, not 3,
# so the epsilon in ndr_resolve_for_pitch is doing real work.
#
# Expected at the end: dump_ndr reports the PER-LAYER quantization (a rule
# no longer has one slot count), check_design is clean, and a value that
# cannot be realized on a governed layer is LOUD at run_detailed_nuts the
# way R3 already is for multipliers.
#
# ORDERING: the track patterns are declared BEFORE the rules here, which
# the multiplier vehicles do not need to do.  That is a real precondition
# rather than a style choice — an absolute value has no meaning without the
# slot geometry it quantizes against, so `def_ndr` refuses one when the
# governed layers have no pattern yet, naming the multiplier form as the
# order-independent alternative.  Resolving later against whatever grid
# happened to exist would silently charge a different width than declared.

add_block blkA 0   0    200 300
add_block blkB 800 0    1000 300
add_block blkC 0   400  200 700
add_block blkD 800 400  1000 700

add_bus fine_[4] blkA.p blkB.q
add_bus wide_[4] blkC.p blkD.q
add_bus dflt_[6] blkA.d blkB.e
# A governed bus that routes VERTICALLY, so its segment lands on the COARSE
# pair (M4/M6, pitch 5.0) rather than the fine one.  Without it the vehicle
# only ever places `fine3` on M3/M5 — where the conservative maximum happens
# to be the right answer — and the per-layer resolution is invisible in the
# routed result.  `fine3`'s width 3 is 2 slots/bit here and 1 there.
add_bus vert_[4] blkA.v blkC.w

def_layer 3 M3 H 20
def_layer 4 M4 V 20
def_layer 5 M5 H TOP 20
def_layer 6 M6 V TOP 20

# MIXED PITCHES — the point of the vehicle.  Per-signal-slot channel cost
# (unit_pitch / n_signal_slots): M3/M5 = 30/12 = 2.5, M4/M6 = 60/12 = 5.0.
# One absolute rule, two slot counts.
def_track_pattern 3 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 5 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 4 0 VDD 4 2 (_ 2 2)x12 GND 4 2
def_track_pattern 6 0 VDD 4 2 (_ 2 2)x12 GND 4 2

# Absolute width/spacing in LAYOUT UNITS (what the script already speaks —
# `corner_margin`, `set_min_stub_length` and the pattern geometry below are
# all in the same unit, and `set_import_scale` is what relates them to µm).
def_ndr fine3  width 3
def_ndr space5 width 4 spacing 5 shield bus net GND
set_ndr fine_ fine3
set_ndr wide_ space5
set_ndr vert_ fine3

run_bundler STRICT --dump
dump_ndr

generate_topologies
set_track_pitch 3
run_planner 1

run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
dump_ndr
check_design
report_wirelength
